# Beat (week 5, Thursday) — the parent waits up. cast.md § 3.1: "We love you"
# precedes correction framed as encouragement and "have you been keeping up
# with your meetings?"; tearful when the player "seems distant"; "I was
# talking to Brother Phillips". Plays if the player has missed a meeting
# this month or doubt has begun to show.
# TODO: authenticity check

{GameState.parent_word} is waiting up when you get home. The good lamp is on.
if GameState.skipped_this_month() > 0 or DoubtMeter.value >= 30:
	"Sit with me a minute."
	"I was talking to Brother Phillips. He asked how you were doing. I told him you were fine." A pause. "You are fine. Aren't you?"
	"We love you. You know that. That's the only reason I'm asking."
	- "I'm fine. Just tired."
		"Of course. Of course you are." They turn the lamp off. In the dark: "Your meeting clothes are still in the dryer."
	- "I've had some questions lately." | [if DoubtMeter.noticing >= 25] [else=disable alt_text=""]
		[signal arg="STANDING:family:-3"]
		[signal arg="RELIEF:1"]
		[signal arg="FLAG:told_parent_questions"]
		A long quiet. "Questions are fine. Everybody has questions. That's what the meetings are for."
		They take your hand. "Promise me you'll bring them to the meetings. Not — anywhere else."
else:
	"Come sit a minute. I won't keep you."
	"I don't say it enough. I'm proud of you. The way you've kept on." Their eyes are wet, and they laugh at themselves for it. "Look at me."
	- "Thanks, {GameState.parent_word}."
		[signal arg="STANDING:family:1"]
		They pat the couch cushion twice, which means go to bed, and you do.
	- Just sit with them.
		[signal arg="STANDING:family:2"]
		You sit until the news comes on. They don't turn it up. After a while their head tips onto your shoulder.
